    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n101 Ardoyne House is a 10th-floor apartment in the heart of Dublin 4, boasting spectacular views over Dublin City and the surrounding villages of Ballsbridge and Donnybrook, taking in the iconic Pigeon House chimneys and Dublin Bay. Extending to a generous size, this bright and spacious home offers the discerning purchaser a superb opportunity to create a truly exceptional residence in one of Dublin's most sought-after locations. While the apartment requires refurbishment and modernisation throughout, it benefits from a well-proportioned layout and outstanding potential to put your own stamp on the property. Beautifully landscaped communal gardens surround Ardoyne House, further enhancing its appeal.\n\nArdoyne House, built in 1961, is ideally located in the heart of Ballsbridge adjacent to Herbert Park, one of Dublin's most scenic and renowned parks. The city centre is approximately a fifteen-minute walk away, while the vibrant villages of Ballsbridge, Donnybrook and Ranelagh are all within easy walking distance, offering an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants and shops. The accommodation comprises a bright entrance hallway, a large living room and kitchen, three bedrooms, a principal bedroom with en-suite, and a separate shower room. Requiring complete refurbishment throughout, this property presents a rare opportunity to create a bespoke home with breathtaking views in a prime Dublin 4 setting. Viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall: - \nA spacious and bright entrance hall provides a warm welcome and creates an excellent sense of space upon entering the apartment.\n\nLiving room: - \nA cosy and inviting living room enjoying fabulous views over Herbert Park, creating a wonderful sense of space and tranquillity.\n\nKitchen: - \nThe kitchen is fitted with built-in wall and floor presses, together with an integrated oven, hob, extractor fan and dishwasher. The walls are partially tiled, and the boiler is conveniently located within the kitchen.\n\nBedroom 1: - \nA bright double bedroom with a built-in wardrobe and pleasant views over Ballsbridge.\n\nMain Bedroom: - \nA bright and spacious main bedroom enjoying lovely natural light and benefiting from a built-in wardrobe.\n\nEnsuite: - \nWell-appointed bathroom fitted with a bath/shower, w.c. and wash hand basin. The walls are tiled, and the room benefits from generous storage space.\n\nBedroom 3: - \nA lovely double bedroom with built-in storage and fabulous views over Dublin City.\n\nMain bathroom: - \nShower room fitted with a shower, w.c. and wash hand basin. There is a storage cabinet housing the washing machine with space for a dryer, while the tiled walls provide a practical finish. The room also benefits from excellent additional storage space.\n\n"
      },
      {
